      "id": "plaid-internal-mcp-server--summary",
      "approach_id": "plaid-internal-mcp-server",
      "field": "summary",
      "text": "Plaid's central internal Model Context Protocol server. Plaid built it because third-party MCP servers could not reach its internal data. The server integrates more than 20 tools and several internal services such as Jira, application logs, and data schemas, behind Plaid's identity-aware proxy and centralized authorization. Plaid reports thousands of tool calls and dozens of agents built on the server. Separately, Claude Code and Cursor are used by more than 80% of Plaid engineers; server adoption is not quantified.",
      "kind": "fact",
      "provenance": "reported",
      "confidence": "high",
      "confidence_reason": "A linked first-party source states the claim.",
      "valid_at": null,
      "evidence": [
